 "response": "Getosti's budget is **$2,254K**. I worked through the records by hand, so small arithmetic slips across ~1,000 entries are possible.\n\n**Method**\n\n1. I ignored every message not from the Finance Office (Sales, PMO, Engineering, Facilities and the rest). Non-budget Finance notes such as room moves, audits and cost-center codes have no effect.\n2. I settled each withdrawal from the latest record back to the earliest. A withdrawal only counts if no later withdrawal cancels it, and long chains are followed to the end. For example:\n   - #1164 withdraws #0154, which revives #0021. #0021 withdraws #0013, which revives #0012. #0012 withdraws #0003, so #0003 does not count.\n   - #1438 withdraws #0784, which revives #0708. #0708 withdraws #0534, which revives #0165. #0165 withdraws #0033, so #0033 does not count.\n   - #1250 withdraws #0150, which revives #0087. #0087 withdraws #0080, so #0071 still counts.\n3. I added up every Finance Office budget update and then removed the ones that end up withdrawn.\n\n**Totals**\n\n- Starting budget (#0001): $1,730K.\n- All Finance Office increases and decreases after that: net +$3,272K, which gives $5,002K.\n- 120 of those updates end up withdrawn. Together they add up to a net +$2,748K, so that amount comes off.\n- $5,002K \u2212 $2,748K = **$2,254K**.\n\nANSWER: $2254K",
